  "Number": 14,
  "Question": "The sum of the numerical coefficients in the complete expansion of \\((x^2-2xy+y^2)^7\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0\\)",
    "B": "\\(7\\)",
    "C": "\\(14\\)",
    "D": "\\(128\\)",
    "E": "\\(128^2\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Setting \\(x=y=1\\) turns each expanded term \\(c x^i y^j\\) into its numerical coefficient \\(c\\), including its sign. Thus this substitution adds all the coefficients without requiring the expansion.\n\nThe required sum is\n\\[\n(1^2-2\\cdot1\\cdot1+1^2)^7\n=(1-2+1)^7=0.\n\\]\nTherefore the sum is \\(0\\), choice A.",
